## Reference identities (ImplementationPlan.md 5.11.2, M21.a item 5; texts of
## 5.11.9). An identity is the Assembly row's name, version and culture and
## the token of its public key (cli::computePublicKeyToken):
## - two files with the same full identity and the same bytes: the first is
##   kept, with the warning
##   '<path> has the same identity as <path> (<identity>); using the first',
##   and the link is the same as with one copy, in either order; a directory
##   names its files '<dir>/<file>' with '/' on every host (M21 review-r1
##   finding 5), so a pack holding FakeCore.dll and a copy FakeCoreCopy.dll
##   warns about pack/FakeCoreCopy.dll;
## - two files with the same full identity and different contents are the
##   error (section 12 row 2026-10-26, '5.11.2 and 5.11.9 amended (duplicate
##   identities, order independence)')
##   'references <path> and <path> have the same identity (<identity>) but different contents',
##   the paths in ReferenceSet's rank order (the normalized path: one/ before
##   plus/), so the text does not depend on the command-line order;
## - the same simple name with another version, or another key, is the error
##   'references <path> (<identity>) and <path> (<identity>) have the same name but different versions or keys'
##   (no version unification, Roslyn's r15);
## - a binding that lands in a System.Private.* assembly without
##   [assembly: ReferenceAssembly] (an implementation assembly, as in a
##   runtime's shared framework directory) gives the warning
##   '<path> is not a reference assembly; binding '<Ns.Type>' to <identity> ties the output to one runtime build',
##   and still binds; the same type from a reference assembly gives none,
##   and so does each condition alone: an assembly without
##   [ReferenceAssembly] whose name is not System.Private.* (FakeThreadingImpl)
##   and a System.Private.* reference assembly (System.Private.FakeLibRef).
## FakeInterop, FakeInteropV9 (9.0.0.0) and FakeInteropK2 (token
## 31bf3856ad364e35 instead of b03f5f7f11d50a3a) are all named FakeInterop;
## FakeInteropExtra has FakeInterop's Assembly row and one more type;
## System.Private.FakeLib defines Interlocked without [ReferenceAssembly]
## (Inputs/fakepack/FakeThreading.il, variant PRIVATE), FakeThreadingImpl
## (variant NOREFASM) is FakeThreading without it, and
## System.Private.FakeLibRef (variant PRIVREF) is System.Private.FakeLib with
## it.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj p1.ll -o p1.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj fence.ll -o fence.o
# RUN: mkdir base one two v9 k2 priv plus pack impl privref
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o base/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeThreading.yaml -o base/FakeThreading.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInterop.yaml -o one/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInterop.yaml -o two/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInteropV9.yaml -o v9/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInteropK2.yaml -o k2/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeInteropExtra.yaml -o plus/FakeInterop.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o priv/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/System.Private.FakeLib.yaml -o priv/System.Private.FakeLib.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o impl/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeThreadingImpl.yaml -o impl/FakeThreading.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/FakeCore.yaml -o privref/FakeCore.dll
# RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/fakepack/System.Private.FakeLibRef.yaml -o privref/System.Private.FakeLib.dll

# DEFINE: %{fc} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"

## One copy.
# RUN: mkdir single dup dup-rev
# RUN: msil-ld p1.o --reference=base --reference=one/FakeInterop.dll -o single/prog.exe 2>&1 | count 0

## Two copies with one identity: a warning naming the second, and the same
## PE.
# RUN: msil-ld p1.o --reference=base --reference=one/FakeInterop.dll --reference=two/FakeInterop.dll \
# RUN:   -o dup/prog.exe 2>&1 | %{fc} --check-prefix=DUP -DFIRST=one -DSECOND=two \
